<Base title="Terms of Use" description="Terms of Use of Talha M Blog: the rules for reading, sharing and commenting on our content, our newsletter terms, and how copyright takedown requests work.">
  <section class="article-head"><h1>Terms of Use</h1></section>
  <div class="prose">
    <p><em>Last updated: October 15, 2026</em></p>

    <p>Welcome to Talha M Blog (talhablog.com). These Terms of Use explain the rules that apply when you read, share, comment on or otherwise use this website. By opening and using this website, you accept these terms. If you do not agree with them, please do not use the website. We have written these terms in the same simple English we use in our stories, so that every reader can understand them.</p>

    <h2>What this website is</h2>
    <p>Talha M Blog is an independent news and information website. We publish explanations of news stories, background articles and informational posts in simple English. The website is free to read. It is operated by Talha Mehmood, an independent publisher based in Pakistan. Readers do not need an account to read this website. Our interactive features — the comments under each story and our email newsletter — are optional and are explained in these terms and in our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

    <h2>Who may use the interactive features</h2>
    <p>Anyone may read this website. The interactive features — posting comments and subscribing to the newsletter — are intended for readers aged 13 and over. If you are under 13, please do not post comments or subscribe to the newsletter; enjoy the stories with a parent or guardian instead. By posting a comment or subscribing, you confirm that the name and email address you give are your own, or that you have permission to use them.</p>

    <h2>Using our content</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You may read all articles on this website freely, for your own personal use and learning.</li>
      <li>You may share links to our articles anywhere — on social media, in messages, or on your own website. Sharing links is welcome and helps us.</li>
      <li>You may quote a short part of an article, if you clearly name Talha M Blog as the source and include a working link back to the original article.</li>
      <li>You may not copy a full article, or a large part of one, and publish it somewhere else as if it were your own work.</li>
      <li>You may not sell our articles, or use them inside a paid product, without written permission from us first.</li>
      <li>The Talha M Blog name, and the illustrations published on this website, belong to Talha M Blog unless a page clearly says otherwise. News facts themselves belong to everyone; the words and pictures we create to explain them are ours.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Comments</h2>
    <p>Most stories on this website have a comments section, so readers can discuss the story. To comment, you write your name and email address and your comment text. Your name and comment are shown publicly on the page; your email address is never shown publicly. The <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> explains what comment information is stored, where, and how you can ask for a comment to be deleted.</p>
    <p>When you post a comment, you agree to these rules:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Be respectful. Disagreement is welcome; abuse, hate speech and personal attacks are not.</li>
      <li>Do not post anything unlawful, threatening, defamatory or misleading, and do not post rumours about a person as if they were proven facts.</li>
      <li>Do not post spam, advertisements, or repeated copies of the same comment.</li>
      <li>Do not pretend to be another person, and do not post another person's private information, such as their phone number, address or email.</li>
      <li>Do not post text or images that belong to someone else unless you have their permission.</li>
      <li>You are responsible for your own comments, for their content and for any result of posting them.</li>
      <li>By posting a comment, you give Talha M Blog permission to display it on this website, with your chosen name, for as long as the story remains published.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Comments are moderated. We may hold, edit for obvious abuse, hide or delete any comment that breaks these rules, and we may block repeat offenders from commenting. We are not required to publish every comment, and a decision about a comment is final. If you believe a comment about you is unfair or unlawful, email us and we will review it, as described on our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.</p>

    <h2>Newsletter</h2>
    <p>Readers may subscribe to our free email newsletter on story pages. Subscribing works in two steps: you enter your email address, and then you confirm it by clicking the link in the confirmation email we send you (this is called double opt-in, and it stops other people subscribing your address without your knowledge). The newsletter is sent through Kit, our email provider.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>The newsletter contains our new stories and, rarely, an important website announcement. Nothing else.</li>
      <li>Every newsletter email contains an unsubscribe link. One click removes your address, free of charge, at any time.</li>
      <li>We never sell or rent subscriber email addresses. How subscriber information is handled is explained in the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
      <li>We may change or stop the newsletter service at any time. If we stop it, subscribers' addresses will be deleted from the newsletter list.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Information, not professional advice</h2>
    <p>Everything published on Talha M Blog is provided for general information and education only. Our articles are summaries and explanations of news and publicly available information. They are not legal, medical, financial or any other kind of professional advice, and they must not be treated as a replacement for advice from a qualified professional. For decisions that matter to your health, money, legal position or safety, always consult a qualified professional or an official source. Our <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> explains this in more detail.</p>

    <h2>Accuracy and changes to articles</h2>
    <p>We work hard to check facts before publishing and to keep articles accurate and up to date. Even so, news develops quickly: officials correct earlier statements, courts change decisions, companies revise figures, and early reports sometimes turn out to be incomplete. For that reason we cannot promise that every detail of every article is complete and current at every moment. When we learn that an article needs a correction or an important update, we change it and show an "Updated" date on the article. The version of an article shown on this website is the latest version we have published, and it replaces any earlier version of the same article.</p>

    <h2>Fair and lawful use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Do not use this website for any unlawful purpose.</li>
      <li>Do not attempt to break, overload, scan or gain unauthorised access to this website, its server or its accounts.</li>
      <li>Do not copy the website's content automatically in bulk in a way that harms the website's operation. Normal search engines indexing our public pages are welcome.</li>
      <li>Do not pretend to be Talha M Blog, or use our name in a way that could mislead readers into thinking a page, account or product is ours when it is not.</li>
      <li>Do not use the comments or any form on this website to send spam or mass unsolicited messages.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Copyright and takedown requests</h2>
    <p>We write our articles in our own words and create our own illustrations. If you believe that any text or image on this website uses your material without permission, you may send us a takedown request by email to <a href="mailto:contact@talhablog.com">contact@talhablog.com</a> with the subject "Copyright". Please include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your full name, and the name of the owner of the material if that is not you.</li>
      <li>The exact link (URL) of the page on talhablog.com where the material appears.</li>
      <li>A short description of your material and, if possible, a link to where it was first published.</li>
      <li>A statement that you own the material, or are authorised to act for the owner, and that its use on this website is not permitted.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We aim to reply to complete requests within a few working days. If a request checks out, we will remove or correct the material as quickly as we reasonably can. If you sent a request by mistake, or you later give permission, email us again and we will restore the material where appropriate.</p>

    <h2>External links</h2>
    <p>Our articles link to other websites as sources and for further reading. Those websites belong to their own owners, run under their own terms, and can change without our knowledge. A link from Talha M Blog is not an endorsement of everything on the linked website, and we are not responsible for the content, accuracy or policies of external websites.</p>

    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>This website has applied to display advertising provided by Google AdSense and similar services, and advertisements will appear once the application is approved. Advertisements are chosen automatically by the advertising provider. An advertisement appearing on Talha M Blog does not mean that we recommend the advertised product or company, and any dealing you have with an advertiser is between you and that advertiser. Readers from Europe and some US states are shown a consent message about advertising cookies before such cookies are used; information about advertising cookies and your choices can be found in our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

    <h2>Availability of the website</h2>
    <p>We try to keep Talha M Blog online and working at all times, but we cannot guarantee uninterrupted access. The website may occasionally be unavailable because of maintenance, technical problems or reasons outside our control. We may also change, move or remove articles, categories or parts of the website at any time.</p>

    <h2>Limitation of responsibility</h2>
    <p>To the extent allowed by law, Talha M Blog and its operator are not responsible for any loss or damage that results from relying on information published on this website, from the website being unavailable, or from the content of external websites linked from here. Readers use the information on this website at their own judgement. Nothing in these terms removes any responsibility that cannot legally be removed.</p>

    <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>We may update these Terms of Use from time to time, for example when we add a new feature. When we do, the revised terms will be posted on this page with a new "Last updated" date, and they will apply from that date onward. By continuing to use the website after a change, you accept the updated terms.</p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>These terms are governed by the laws of Pakistan. If any part of these terms is found to be unenforceable, the remaining parts continue to apply in full.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>If you have any question about these Terms of Use, please contact us through our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a> or by email at <a href="mailto:contact@talhablog.com">contact@talhablog.com</a>.</p>
  </div>
